# PolyKernel Todo 23 (Wave 4): gfx942 NO-RUN NEGATIVE — QA log (GRACEFUL DEVICE-NOT-FOUND)
# Host: Linux 7.1.4-1-cachyos x86_64   Date: 2026-07-27T10:05:00Z
# Local GPU: AMD Radeon RX 7800 XT (Navi 32) = gfx1101   ROCm/clr: 7.2.3
# Probe:   a gfx942 binary (gfx942 code object embedded, NO gfx1101 code object)
# Verdict: PASS — running a gfx942 binary locally reports "no gfx942 device,
#          compile-only" GRACEFULLY (checked hipGetDeviceCount/hipGetDeviceProperties
#          device-not-found path, exit 0), NOT a crash or a doomed launch.
##############################################################################

=== WHAT THIS PROVES ===
The happy path (reports/mi300_compile.log) shows gfx942 cross-compiles clean. This
negative shows the OTHER half of the contract: because there is NO MI300 on this
host (local GPU = gfx1101), a gfx942 binary must NOT be launched. The runtime guard
enumerates HIP devices, looks for a gfx942 by gcnArchName, and on finding none
reports "compile-only" and exits 0 — a checked device-not-found path. This is the
exact guard the bench (Todo 25) uses to skip gfx942 runs until the W5 rental.

=== PROBE (scratch, not a deliverable: /tmp/opencode/gfx942_norun_probe.hip.cpp) ===
A trivial __global__ kernel + a host main that:
  1. hipGetDeviceCount(&count)            — checked; hipSuccess here (1 device).
  2. hipGetDeviceProperties per device    — prints name + gcnArchName.
  3. searches for a device whose gcnArchName contains "gfx942".
  4. if none -> prints "no gfx942 device, compile-only ..." and returns 0 (graceful).
The kernel is NEVER launched locally — the device check gates it (a launch of the
gfx942 code object on the gfx1101 device would be a launch error; we avoid it).

=== COMMANDS ===
nix develop --impure --accept-flake-config -c bash -c '
  hipcc --offload-arch=gfx942 /tmp/opencode/gfx942_norun_probe.hip.cpp \
        -o /tmp/opencode/gfx942_norun_probe        # embed a gfx942 code object
  /tmp/opencode/gfx942_norun_probe                 # run on the gfx1101 host
'

=== OUTPUT ===
+ hipcc --offload-arch=gfx942 /tmp/opencode/gfx942_norun_probe.hip.cpp -o /tmp/opencode/gfx942_norun_probe
COMPILE_EXIT=0                       # gfx942 code object built clean (compile-only)

